nemia: No direct evidence (e.g., reticulocytosis, Coombs test not mentioned)", "Diabetic ketoacidosis: Glucose within normal range, no metabolic acidosis detected (HCO3- 22 mEq/L)"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional symptoms (fever, night sweats, weight loss)", "Pancytopenia with blast involvement", "Sudden visual acuity deterioration in a diabetic patient"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.4120604688332446, "posterior": 0.30433627963414744, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The high blast percentage and pancytopenia are classic features of myeloid neoplasms. This provides moderate evidence for myeloid leukemia over lymphoid proces…"], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.04, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of lymphoid markers in a high-blast setting strongly argues against ALL as the primary diagnosis."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.07032498668087375, "posterior": 0.053803648448901134, "danger": 0.6, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Subacute presentation is more typical of blast crisis in CML than de novo AML, but absence of chronic phase features weakens this